{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/768964-question-on-favored-prey","id":768964,"title":"Question on favored prey","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-18T22:10:42-08:00","id":768964,"title":"Question on favored prey","content":"I'm just getting into werewolf and reading the splat, so forgive me if this is something obvious I'm not getting.<br /> <br /> Okay, so each of the five tribes has a favored prey that they tend to hunt. The flavor from the books suggests that generally they don't hunt each other's prey, and if they do, the others get pissed. This seems weird to me, given the setting. Ignoring that a lot of packs have dudes from multiple tribes, even if there's a pack that's all one tribe, if an uppity human starts making bad juju in a pack's territory, am I really supposed to believe they'll leave it alone because they're Blood Talons and they hunt other werewolves, and humans are Iron Master territory?<br /> <br /> Like I don't think packs share territory, do they? That's half the point. Keep your own shit clean, or other dudes are gonna see that you're weak and move in on your pack. If I'm a werewolf I'm going to hunt whoever or whatever is on my territory that I need to in order to keep everything pretty secure and in order.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6337-someguywithakatana","name":"someguywithakatana","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T22:15:15-08:00","id":768968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>someguywithakatana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/768964-question-on-favored-prey#post768964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The flavor from the books suggests that generally they don't hunt each other's prey, and if they do, the others get pissed. This seems weird to me, given the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>It should seem weird, as that's not really something the book tries to suggest. No one's going to get pissed over a pack hunting any of the favored prey, though they would probably get pissed if some other pack came into their territory to hunt without warning.<br /> <br /> What part of the flavor from the book suggested this to you?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T22:22:50-08:00","id":768969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/768964-question-on-favored-prey?p=768968#post768968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It should seem weird, as that's not really something the book tries to suggest. No one's going to get pissed over a pack hunting any of the favored prey, though they would probably get pissed if some other pack came into their territory to hunt without warning.<br /> <br /> What part of the flavor from the book suggested this to you?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm looking at second edition, which might be the issue. I never read through 1e, so it may not be there.<br /> <br /> In the segments on the different tribes, where you get the tribe members giving quotes on the others, there's a lot of references to tribes getting pissy about one of the others killing one of their prey. The example that jumps to mind is an Iron Master telling a Storm Lord &quot;Hey, it was pale and it drank blood. How was I supposed to know that it was a guy possessed by a leech spirit.&quot; Implying, of course, that the Storm Lord is pissed that the Iron Master kill-stole. Or something? Like I said, it's weird. And there are other moments like that throughout 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6337-someguywithakatana","name":"someguywithakatana","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T22:40:15-08:00","id":768973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>someguywithakatana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/768964-question-on-favored-prey?p=768969#post768969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm looking at second edition, which might be the issue. I never read through 1e, so it may not be there.</div> </div> </div> </div>The tribal prey angle is an element new to 2e that helps somewhat with differentiating tribes from auspices at a glance and makes managing the game's large numbers of antagonist categories less daunting. Back when 2e was fresh we had a lot of people thinking the tribal prey were exclusive focuses rather than areas of specialty as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the segments on the different tribes, where you get the tribe members giving quotes on the others, there's a lot of references to tribes getting pissy about one of the others killing one of their prey. The example that jumps to mind is an Iron Master telling a Storm Lord &quot;Hey, it was pale and it drank blood. How was I supposed to know that it was a guy possessed by a leech spirit.&quot; Implying, of course, that the Storm Lord is pissed that the Iron Master kill-stole. Or something? Like I said, it's weird. And there are other moments like that throughout 2e. </div> </div> </div>The tribes get Gift affinities and focuses that lend themselves best to hunting their favored prey and this tends to make them cagey about yielding the lead to other tribes in collaboration. It's a matter of specialist pride rather than dogmatic role-enforcement; if you've got a typical mixed pack dealing with a spiritual issue then deferring to the Bone Shadow's expertise is good sense and putting the Iron Master or the Blood Talon in charge of that case instead is infuriatingly nonsensical without some particular reason for the exception.<br /> <br /> All in all, you described how things tend to go from pack-to-pack fairly succinctly:<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If I'm a werewolf I'm going to hunt whoever or whatever is on my territory that I need to in order to keep everything pretty secure and in order. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T22:44:59-08:00","id":768976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/768964-question-on-favored-prey?p=768973#post768973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The tribal prey angle is an element new to 2e that helps somewhat with differentiating tribes from auspices at a glance and makes managing the game's large numbers of antagonist categories less daunting. Back when 2e was fresh we had a lot of people thinking the tribal prey were exclusive focuses rather than areas of specialty as well.<br /> <br /> The tribes get Gift affinities and focuses that lend themselves best to hunting their favored prey and this tends to make them cagey about yielding the lead to other tribes in collaboration. It's a matter of specialist pride rather than dogmatic role-enforcement; if you've got a typical mixed pack dealing with a spiritual issue then deferring to the Bone Shadow's expertise is good sense and putting the Iron Master or the Blood Talon in charge of that case instead is infuriatingly nonsensical without some particular reason for the exception.<br /> <br /> All in all, you described how things tend to go from pack-to-pack fairly succinctly:</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, that makes WAAAAAY more sense. To a point I'm kind of embarrassed that I didn't piece it together myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6337-someguywithakatana","name":"someguywithakatana","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T22:48:21-08:00","id":768978,"title":"","content":"While I can imagine some Storm Lord being annoyed that an Iron Master stole his thunder (hoho), Favored Prey represents just that, a favored prey. The tribes specialize, focus and prioritize a particular prey, but it's not under their sole purview. I mean, a pack with no Hunters in Darkness aren't just gonna let the Shartha run free in their territory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T00:22:27-08:00","id":769020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/768964-question-on-favored-prey?p=768978#post768978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, a pack with no Hunters in Darkness aren't just gonna let the Shartha run free in their territory.</div> </div> </div> </div>BUT if they <i><b>have</b></i> a Hunter in Darkness in pack, he will at least advice on the Hunt if not directly lead it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-19-2015, 03:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T05:05:05-08:00","id":769118,"title":"","content":"I imagine the quote is less about, 'You stole my kill' and more about, 'We brought stakes and fire to fight a Claimed.' Especially when the reference is to the Storm Lords.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}